terrads_d0e8038f5df2_manualfix,Zenodo/TerraDS,iac_benchmark/scenarios_greenfield/terrads_d0e8038f5df2,True,True,0,0,0,0,0,,manual-fix,terrads_d0e8038f5df2,"Same self-containment gap class as terrads_d72f6bbf765a/terrads_a2f8e4e2513d, a third independent instance: 'logging_bucket' fed an aws_s3_bucket_logging target_bucket with no backing aws_s3_bucket resource. Defaulted it to '' and added a real second bucket (with public-access-block + BucketOwnerPreferred ownership controls, the minimum S3 access-logging requires of its target) that a new local.effective_logging_bucket falls back to. Also added a default for 'region' (used only for KMS/tagging, never independently validated) and removed a pre-existing 'lifecycle { prevent_destroy = true }' on the main CloudTrail bucket -- this project's own deploy-check cell always tears every stack down after testing, and prevent_destroy would have blocked that the same way Cognito's deletion_protection did in an earlier documented case (see 'Deprecated/deleted flags that now block teardown, not creation' in the Terraform L5-backlog notes). Verified with a full plan: 'Plan: 12 to add, 0 to change, 0 to destroy' (only pre-existing lifecycle-configuration deprecation warnings).",370.0,2326.0,12.0,8.0,4.0,"aws_caller_identity, aws_iam_policy_document, aws_kms_alias, aws_kms_key, aws_partition, aws_s3_bucket, aws_s3_bucket_lifecycle_configuration, aws_s3_bucket_logging, aws_s3_bucket_ownership_controls, aws_s3_bucket_policy, aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block, aws_s3_bucket_server_side_encryption_configuration, aws_s3_bucket_versioning",True,237.0,
